                <pb facs="0495" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg407"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Meyer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-04-18"><hi rendition="#italic">April 18,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 211.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 339, of the 4th
                    ultimo, I have to say that the Acting Attorney-General of the United States
                    states that he has forwarded to the United States attorney for the northern
                    district of Ohio the papers relating to the apparently fraudulent naturalization
                    of Giuseppe Divito, with instructions to investigate the case and, if the
                    evidence is obtainable, to institute criminal proceedings against the persons
                    involved.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
